On the other hand, with the advancement of scientific possibilities and the gradual disappearance of many prohibitions on thinking, some beautiful and gratifying developments are emerging: the confirmation of ancient knowledge through new scientific research results!

For example, a large-scale study by the Dutch cardiologist Pim van Lommel, who systematically investigated and evaluated near-death experiences, produced the result, sensational by today's standards, that human consciousness can exist independently of the body - which confirms the ancient knowledge of a soul connected to the body and independent of it (GrailWorld reported on this in issue 49).

Fritz-Albert Popp also provided evidence that living cells emit light, for which he was initially met with considerable hostility until the phenomenon could no longer be denied. This also fits in with the old knowledge of the existence of an aura, a ring of radiation that surrounds everything living and can be seen without further ado by clairvoyant people (see GralsWelt 58).

Rupert Sheldrake's first-class study on the "Seventh Sense of Animals" can also be considered very valuable with regard to the effect of "otherworldly" influences - such as forms of thought and sensation or the work of natural beings - regardless of what name one gives the observed phenomena.

Much depends on whether we can get used to the idea of ​​subtle worlds lying above us as part of the great overall creation. We cannot see them directly, but we experience their effects all the time, as they literally "spill over" into the gross material world that we can see. Only in this way can we finally find logical, comprehensible and plausible explanations for many phenomena that would have remained a mystery to our previous view, which was fixated on the purely material.

It is high time for a new synthesis of holistic, spiritual knowledge and a new science that is prepared to leave the narrow, very limited and thus one-sided, purely material world view.

And if we look with open minds at all the areas in which animals can help us, which they are certainly happy to do, then one thing is certain: a higher appreciation, a more respectful and loving treatment of our fellow creatures, who could become our best friends!



